_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 38
---
order: 38
---
short_label: VII.38
---
statement: If a number has any part whatever, then it is measured by a number called by the same name as the part.
---
proof:

Let the number *A* have any part whatever, *B,* and let *C* be a number called by the same name as the part *B.*

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="250" height="170" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="VII.38 diagram" src="propVII38.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
